      {
        "heading": "Essence Analysis",
        "body": "The essence account distinguishes full from partial essence. Full generic essence is directly identified with generalized identity, while partial essence is explained through conjunctive structure: something is partly what G is when it appears as a conjunct in what it is to be G. This lets the authors preserve the intuition that essence is more than necessity while also explaining why essentialist claims can resemble real definitions.",
