        "body": "One payoff is that ground-theoretic status is preserved under factual identity, because generalized identity is governed by identity-like structural principles. Another is that grounding implies an essence-based necessitation pattern: if being F grounds being G, then being G is being F or some H, which yields the modal result that F necessitates G. The necessity is derived from essence, not merely stipulated.",
