{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p verification/example_site/spaces/metaphysics/runs/run-20260426T151752Z--cmqk6ysimv/semantic && cat > verification/example_site/spaces/metaphysics/runs/run-20260426T151752Z--cmqk6ysimv/semantic/topic_generation.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"topics\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-grounding-essence-and-necessitation\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Grounding, Essence, and Necessitation\\\",\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Core synthesis\\\",\n          \\\"content\\\": \\\"One source argues that full grounding metaphysically necessitates what is grounded by appeal to cognitive significance and Fine-style essence, while the generalized-identity source explains grounding-to-necessitation patterns through what it is to be the grounded property or fact. The shared topic is not merely that grounding entails necessity, but that essence-like structure is used to explain why the entailment is metaphysically secure.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Key tension\\\",\n          \\\"content\\\": \\\"The sources also warn against reducing essence to modal entailment or equivalence: grounding necessity may follow from essential truths, but necessary coextension alone does not determine essential structure.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Page angle\\\",\n          \\\"content\\\": \\\"A concept page could compare essence-first routes to grounding necessity with generalized-identity routes that derive necessitation while preserving distinctions among full essence, partial essence, and mere necessary equivalence.\\\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-grounding-and-essence-can-both-be-analyzed-in-terms-of-generalized-identity-yiel--e2abdab353f9\\\",\n        \\\"claim-if-being-f-grounds-being-g-then-the-fact-that-being-f-necessitates-being-g-can-b--685ae4dcbfb4\\\",\n        \\\"claim-necessary-entailment-or-equivalence-is-not-sufficient-for-essence-because-genera--162946956228\\\",\n        \\\"claim-full-generic-essence-is-captured-by-generalized-identity-being-f-is-what-it-is-t--96f5798ed301\\\",\n        \\\"claim-partial-generic-essence-is-captured-by-conjunctive-partial-generalized-identity--13ec1cd27c1f\\\",\n        \\\"claim-if-a-fact-p-is-fully-grounded-in-a-plurality-of-facts-d-then-the-conjunction-of--dbb969101dbd\\\",\n        \\\"claim-connecting-questions-lack-cognitive-significance-only-when-fine-style-essential--f96bc70d5d2d\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-conjunction-of-the-significance-principle-the-essence-principle-and-the-meta--4f212a9f1869\\\",\n        \\\"claim-grounding-necessity-is-not-secured-merely-by-treating-grounding-as-a-determinati--23325d0a6e99\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\\\",\n        \\\"source-01-grounding-necessary-or-contingent--6e8195a096f0\\\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-formal-structure-of-grounding\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Formal Structure of Grounding Relations\\\",\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Core synthesis\\\",\n          \\\"content\\\": \\\"The generalized-identity source offers formal analyses of grounding through disjunctive parthood, quasi-subsumption, and preservation under factual identity. The strict-order source instead challenges familiar structural assumptions by arguing that grounding is not transitive, irreflexive, or asymmetric.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Key tension\\\",\n          \\\"content\\\": \\\"Together the sources make the formal profile of grounding a live issue: grounding may need a precise structural account, but that account cannot simply assume the strict-order behavior often associated with fundamentality.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Page angle\\\",\n          \\\"content\\\": \\\"A page could map candidate formal constraints on grounding and explain how identity-preservation, parthood, subsumption, non-transitivity, reflexivity, and symmetry claims pull in different directions.\\\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-factual-grounding-is-analyzed-through-disjunctive-parthood-a-plurality-of-facts--d0a2dc4b2f48\\\",\n        \\\"claim-a-subsumption-theoretic-version-of-grounding-says-that-p1-p2-and-so-on-ground-q--fe650fc0cecd\\\",\n        \\\"claim-ground-theoretic-status-is-preserved-under-factual-identity-because-the-proposed--4aecebbdb4a2\\\",\n        \\\"claim-generalized-identity-is-a-non-factive-no-difference-operator-that-can-apply-to-f--7cb985988184\\\",\n        \\\"claim-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order-because-it-is-neither-transitive-irreflexive-nor--0dc6a102d51b\\\",\n        \\\"claim-truthmaking-is-non-transitive-socrates-being-white-truthmakes-the-proposition-th--3fbb8a3c9b9d\\\",\n        \\\"claim-alethic-fact-grounding-is-non-irreflexive-because-if-proposition-b-is-true-and-s--0f3a01a46967\\\",\n        \\\"claim-truthmaking-and-alethic-fact-grounding-are-non-asymmetric-because-distinct-propo--9d116dfbb4b5\\\",\n        \\\"claim-grounding-does-not-entail-being-more-fundamental-than-so-appeals-to-relative-fun--0468a01c8a45\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\\\",\n        \\\"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\\\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-truthmaking-facts-and-nonfactive-identity\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Truthmaking, Facts, and Non-Factive Identity\\\",\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Core synthesis\\\",\n          \\\"content\\\": \\\"The truthmaking source treats truthmaking and alethic-fact grounding as species of grounding, including cases where truthmakers ground truth facts. The generalized-identity source supplies a non-factive no-difference operator that can apply to factual and generic contents without taking fact-shaped or property-shaped entities as relata.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Key tension\\\",\n          \\\"content\\\": \\\"This makes a synthesis-worthy topic because both sources connect grounding with facts and truth, but they place different pressure on the ontology of relata: one develops grounding through truthmakers and truth facts, while the other tries to formulate grounding and essence without requiring such entities as the basic relata.\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Page angle\\\",\n          \\\"content\\\": \\\"A page could compare entity-based truthmaker grounding with content-based generalized identity, noting that the available evidence supports a conceptual contrast rather than a direct refutation between the approaches.\\\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-generalized-identity-is-a-non-factive-no-difference-operator-that-can-apply-to-f--7cb985988184\\\",\n        \\\"claim-objectual-essence-can-be-accounted-for-through-generic-essence-so-a-feature-is-w--bd5daa95f779\\\",\n        \\\"claim-truthmaking-is-a-species-of-grounding-because-the-relation-between-a-truthmaker--4d84e79d3baf\\\",\n        \\\"claim-alethic-fact-grounding-is-a-species-of-grounding-in-which-a-truthmaker-grounds-t--9c9dc5afedc6\\\",\n        \\\"claim-truthmaking-is-non-irreflexive-because-a-proposition-of-the-form-e-exists-is-mad--d4aca38737b4\\\",\n        \\\"claim-schaffer-s-contrastive-or-differential-formulation-of-grounding-still-fails-to-m--7fd859e88bdc\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"source-03-grounding-essence-and-identity--e857615fb05e\\\",\n        \\\"source-02-grounding-is-not-a-strict-order--7c76f525b4e3\\\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\nJSON\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
